<main id="main"><section class="pageHero compact"><div class="container"><span class="kicker">Legal</span><h1>Acceptable Use Policy</h1><p>Responsible use protects customers, networks and the wider internet.</p></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container legalProse"><h2>Permitted use</h2><p>Services may be used for lawful hosting, development, business systems, private connectivity and other legitimate workloads that do not harm third parties or infrastructure.</p><h2>Prohibited activity</h2><p>You must not use VPN4U services for malware distribution, phishing, credential theft, botnets, unauthorised scanning or intrusion, denial-of-service attacks, spam, deliberate copyright infringement, child sexual abuse material, fraud, threats, unlawful surveillance, trafficking in illegal goods or services, or activity that violates applicable law.</p><h2>Network abuse</h2><p>Activities that materially degrade shared networks, circumvent technical restrictions, spoof network identity for abuse, generate abusive automation or interfere with other customers may be blocked or suspended.</p><h2>VPN use</h2><p>VPN access is a privacy and connectivity tool, not permission to break the law or hide abusive behaviour. Customers remain responsible for activity originating from their accounts.</p><h2>Security incidents</h2><p>If a compromised service is causing harm, we may temporarily isolate, null-route or suspend it while the issue is investigated. We will try to work with the customer where doing so is safe and practical.</p><h2>Reporting</h2><p>Send abuse reports to <a href="mailto:<%= site.emails.abuse %>"><%= site.emails.abuse %></a> with relevant IP addresses, timestamps, logs or evidence.</p></div></section></main>
